##Week 5 Query 
•	New y value: 0.3 – worse than y_best. 
•	First, I will change my length scale and noise levels due to convergence warnings. I assumed the log-likelihood surface was moderately smooth and noisy. This was encoded by a Matern kernel with a minimum length-scale of 0.05 and a WhiteKernel with a relatively high initial noise level and a lower noise bound of 1e-4. The GP repeatedly pushed both the length-scale and noise level to their lower bounds, indicating: the function varies more sharply and locally than my smoothness prior allowed. 
•	I changed length scale from 0.05 to 1e-3 and lower noise bound from 0.3 to 1e-6. 
•	I have also realised that EI should be expressed in the same units as the function. The observed log-likelihood values range from -0.07 to 0.6 and therefore an Xi of 1 was too large and risks distorting the acquisition function rather than promoting meaningful exploration. I change my xi to 0.1 which is scaled to be consistent with the magnitude of the function. It still corresponds to a substantial fraction of the observed output range and therefore still promotes exploration. However, after implementing this new Xi value, the acquisition function was converging prematurely. 
•	I made the decision to switch to UCB to enforce broader exploration. I calculated the UCB beta value based on the GP-UCB confidence parameter and got 5.9. 
•	Even with UCB, the acquisition function still selected the known best basin. To avoid early convergence, it’s important to explore, so I apply a minimum distance of 0.07, corresponding to seven grid steps, which is large enough to prevent repeated sampling. 

